    "body": "<!--\r\n    ❗️❗️❗️ IMPORTANT ❗️❗️❗️\r\n\r\n    DON'T DELETE THIS TEMPLATE! USE IT TO WRITE YOUR ISSUE.\r\n\r\n    If you delete this and you don't give me enough info,\r\n    how would you expect me to solve your issue? Thanks.\r\n\r\n    Also, before posting a new issue, make sure to check the following points!\r\n    You may already find an answer to your problem!\r\n\r\n    ❗️❗️❗️ IMPORTANT ❗️❗️❗️\r\n-->\r\n\r\n- [x] I have read the [Getting Started](https://inappwebview.dev/docs/intro/) section\r\n- [x] I have already searched for the same problem\r\n\r\n## Environment\r\n\r\n| Technology      | Version       |\r\n|-----------------| ------------- |\r\n| Flutter version |    3.3.8           |\r\n| Plugin version  |       [6.0.0-beta.21](https://pub.dev/packages/flutter_inappwebview/versions/6.0.0-beta.21)       |\r\n| Android version |      10         |\r\n| iOS version     |               |\r\n| macOS version   |              |\r\n| Xcode version   |               |\r\n\r\nDevice information: <!-- Manufacturer and model --> xiaomi mix3\r\n\r\n## Description\r\n\r\nThank you so much for developing this flutter library. Overall performance is better than `webview_flutter`. But I have a problem when submitting the app to the app market (Xiaomi App Store). They run a security scan on the application and check that the application gets the list of installed applications at startup (android.permission.MY_READ_INSTALLED_PACKAGES).\r\n\r\n<img width=\"1721\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/8766034/206426188-c3c8cc8a-72dc-4606-85bd-0a178529a3bc.png\">\r\n\r\nIn Xiaomi's view, it is an act of disrespecting user privacy to perform such an operation before the user agrees to the application privacy policy. So they refuse to pass my app.\r\n\r\nSo I would like to ask if it is possible to let WebView be initialized when it is actually used, or provide a method for developers to initialize manually.\r\n\r\n\r\n**Expected behavior:** \r\n\r\nDo not get the list of installed applications when the application starts\r\n\r\n**Current behavior:** \r\n\r\nWhen the app starts, when the user has not agreed to the privacy policy, get the list of installed apps immediately\r\n\r\n## Steps to reproduce\r\n\r\n<!-- Optionally provide the least amount of code that shows this behaviour. -->\r\n\r\n1. This\r\n2. Than that\r\n3. Then\r\n",
